Translation patch: `misc::trusted` (new module: the trust boundary of the packets), lossy UTF-8 and the version regexes

Change: Adds `src/misc/trusted.rs`, declared `pub(crate) mod trusted` in `misc/mod.rs`, with one function per dependency operation, each body being that call: `from_utf8_lossy` (`String::from_utf8_lossy`), `version_re_captures` / `mariadb_version_re_captures` (`captures` of the two version regexes, returning the bytes of groups 1–3), and `btoi_u16` (`btoi::<u16>(b).ok()`). The two regex statics `VERSION_RE` and `MARIADB_VERSION_RE` move there verbatim from `packets/mod.rs`. `RawBytes::as_str` calls `trusted::from_utf8_lossy`; `HandshakePacket::server_version_parsed` / `maria_db_server_version_parsed` become `match trusted::*_version_re_captures(..) { Some((a, b, c)) => Some((btoi_u16(a).unwrap(), ..)), None => None }`. The now-unused imports of `btoi`, `Regex` and `LazyLock` in `packets/mod.rs` are removed. (Patches 68, 70 and 71 add further functions to this module.)
Why: The module is `opaque` in Cargo.toml, so the trusted surface of the packets is exactly this list, each with a Lean model or axiom in `FunsExternal.lean` (the pattern of patch 40). The dependencies cannot be translated (`LazyLock` statics with closures, regex, `String::from_utf8_lossy`).
Behaviour: Identical. `captures.get(i)` is `Some` for groups 1–3 on every match (they are not optional in either pattern), so the `unwrap`s moved into the helper never panic; `.map(|captures| ..)` is the `match`; `btoi_u16(..).unwrap()` panics exactly when `btoi::<u16>(..).unwrap()` does (e.g. on a version with non-ASCII Unicode digits, which `\d` matches); only the panic message changes, from `Result::unwrap` on a `ParseIntegerError` to `Option::unwrap` on `None`.

